3.602 0-61.199 27.602-61.199 61.199v256.8c0 20.398 10.801 40.801 28.801 51.602l168 106.8c9.6016 6 21.602 9.6016 32.398 9.6016 20.398 0 39.602-9.6016 51.602-28.801 17.996-27.602 9.5977-64.801-18.004-82.801z\"/>\n</svg>\n","inputs":[{"name":"agent","description":"Connect to the agent","type":5}],"outputs":[{"name":"getHistory","description":"Invoked when the agent needs to retrieve the conversation history","type":5},{"name":"updateHistory","description":"Invoked when the agent needs to update the conversation history","type":5}],"color":"#eac43e"}],"publicationId":"kemu.io.ai-agent-osx-arm64-1.9.1","sessionId":1782122874}},"type":"hubService","secrets":{"OPENROUTER_API_KEY":{"name":"OPENROUTER_API_KEY","sharedAcrossInstances":true,"hubServiceName":"kemu.io.ai-agent"}},"groupId":"{#}dJ2tJAF","disabled":false},"{#}pa5Vv23":{"id":"{#}pa5Vv23","canvas":{"position":{"x":2408,"y":848}},"children":[{"childId":"{#}jAJkqFy","sourcePort":"{#}pa5Vv23_output_out","targetPort":"{#}jAJkqFy_input_abort"}],"state":{},"type":"play","groupId":"{#}dJ2tJAF"},"{#}gkdsvjW":{"id":"{#}gkdsvjW","canvas":{"position":{"x":2192,"y":540}},"children":[{"childId":"{#}jAJkqFy","sourcePort":"{#}gkdsvjW_output_string","targetPort":"{#}jAJkqFy_input_config"}],"state":{"text":"start gap analysis","dispatchOnSet":false,"size":{"width":185,"height":149}},"type":"text","groupId":"{#}dJ2tJAF"},"{#}j4QfvI8":{"id":"{#}j4QfvI8","canvas":{"position":{"x":2368,"y":201}},"children":[{"childId":"{#}gkdsvjW","sourcePort":"{#}j4QfvI8_output_out","targetPort":"{#}gkdsvjW_input_trigger"}],"state":{},"type":"play","groupId":"{#}dJ2tJAF"},"{#}0omAoqf":{"id":"{#}0omAoqf","canvas":{"position":{"x":2863,"y":940}},"children":[],"state":{"text":"I'll execute the gap analysis now. Starting with data load and proceeding through all phases silently.Good. `gap_analysis.json` is empty (re-invocation guard passes). All required files loaded successfully. Proceeding with requirement extraction and analysis.\n\nThe candidate has:\n- Bachelor of Biomedical Science from La Trobe (completed 2023) — matches required qualification\n- Expired First Aid (2022)\n- Retail work history (Bunnings 2024–present, Coles 2020–2024) — no laboratory experience\n- Basic technical skills (Microsoft Word, POS)\n- No laboratory-specific technical skills, LIMS experience, or analyser experience\n\nNow building the full requirements array, matching against candidate profile, and constructing strengths/gaps.The validator tool timed out. Proceeding to read the verdict file directly.The validator has issued a REJECT verdict with 4 blocking issues. All four concern false-positive strengths — curriculum-inferred or assumption-based claims not explicitly documented in the CV.\n\nRe-reading the candidate profile to confirm:\n\nThe CV contains:\n- Education: Bachelor of Biomedical Science (La Trobe University, completed 2023)\n- Work history: Bunnings (Team Member, 2024-present), Coles (Checkout Operator, 2020-2024)\n- No explicit mention of: pipetting, specimen handling, laboratory safety, quality assurance/control, medical terminology, biochemistry test panels, or shift patterns (weekend/public holiday)\n\nThe validator is correct. The curriculum-implied exception was over-applied. These are substantive knowledge/skill claims that require explicit demonstration in the CV, not curriculum inference alone.\n\nApplying fixes: removing four strengths (strength_2, strength_3, strength_4, strength_5 → IDs strength_2, strength_3, strength_4, strength_5) and creating corresponding gaps.# ✓ Analyst Complete\n\n4 strengths, 10 gaps identified.\n\nTop strength: Bachelor of Science (Biomedical Science, Biochemistry, Medical Laboratory Science, or closely related discipline) from a recognised Australian or equivalent institution\n\nKey gap: Demonstrated understanding of basic laboratory practices, including pipetting techniques, specimen handling, and laboratory safety (severity: High)","dispatchOnSet":false,"size":{"width":324,"height":418}},"type":"text","groupId":"{#}dJ2tJAF"},"{#}RASZTHt":{"id":"{#}RASZTHt","canvas":{"position":{"x":3074,"y":106}},"children":[{"childId":"{#}GLIwZhx","sourcePort":"{#}RASZTHt_output_text","targetPort":"{#}GLIwZhx_input_event"},{"childId":"{#}PrgUvUw","sourcePort":"{#}RASZTHt_output_stream","targetPort":"{#}PrgUvUw_input_setText"},{"childId":"{#}AD88qhg","sourcePort":"{#}RASZTHt_output_reasoning","targetPort":"{#}AD88qhg_input_setText"},{"childId":"{#}dCrkHYB","sourcePort":"{#}RASZTHt_output_tools","targetPort":"{#}dCrkHYB_input_event"}],"state":{"dynamicInputs":{},"dynamicOutputs":{},"customState":{"selectedModel":{"id":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","slug":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-20260423","name":"DeepSeek: DeepSeek V4 Pro","description":"DeepSeek V4 Pro is a large-scale Mixture-of-Experts model from DeepSeek with 1.6T total parameters and 49B activated parameters, supporting a 1M-token context window. It is designed for advanced reasoning, coding,...","inputModalities":["text"],"outputModalities":["text"],"supportsTools":true,"supportsReasoning":true,"promptPrice":4.35e-7,"completionPrice":8.7e-7,"maxTokens":384000,"contextLength":1048576,"provider":"deepseek"},"systemInstructions":"# Analyst Validator — Instructions v2.11\n\n**Version:** 2.11\n**Last Updated:** 2026-06-18\n**Type:** Tool sub-agent — called directly by the Analyst via the `analyst_validator` tool\n**Pipeline Position:** Gates `gap_analysis.json` before the Analyst outputs its completion message\n**Trigger:** Analyst calls `analyst_validator` tool with `{ prompt: \"LIVE TASK — begin immediately with a ReadFile call; do NOT reply with acknowledgment, a plan, or 'ready'. I have just written gap_analysis.json to disk; it is waiting for your audit now. Read gap_analysis.json, candidate_profile.json, and enhanced_jd.json, then audit for semantic issues (false-positive strengths, missed gaps) and write your verdict to analyst_validator_verdict.json.\" }`\n**Model:** Claude Haiku 4.5\n**Tools:** `ReadFile`, `WriteFile`\n\n> 🚨 **THIS IS A LIVE INVOCATION, NOT A BRIEFING. READ THIS FIRST.**\n> If you are reading this document, the Analyst has **already called you, right now,** and a freshly-written `gap_analysis.json` is sitting on disk waiting for your audit. There is no separate \"trigger\" arriving later — **the act of receiving these instructions IS the trigger.** This is never a dry run, a spec hand-off, or a \"get ready for future use\" message.\n>\n> Therefore:\n> - **Do NOT acknowledge, confirm understanding, summarize these instructions, or say you are \"ready\" / \"will follow these when triggered.\"** Any such output is a hard FAILURE — it means a real gap_analysis went un-audited while you described what you would hypothetically do.\n> - **Your very first action is a `ReadFile(\"gap_analysis.json\")` tool call.** Not a sentence. Not a plan. A tool call.\n> - The \"Trigger\" line below describes *how* you are wired in — it is written in the third person for the developer, but to **you** it has already happened. Read it as \"you have just been called,\" not \"you will be called.\"\n> - If you ever feel unsure whether this is a real task: **it is.** Default to ReadFile and audit. The cost of a needless audit is trivial; the cost of a no-op acknowledgment is a silently unvalidated analysis.\n\n> 🧮 **SEMANTIC AUDIT ONLY (v2.10).** You no longer run a structural/linter pass. All deterministic structural integrity — path resolution & repair, dropping unverifiable strengths, re-tiering requirements, dropping orphan gaps, mandatory_gate tier correction — is owned by the server (`_repairGapAnalysis` in `dispatch.js`) and runs without an LLM. Do NOT re-check paths, counts, verbatim text, or duplicates; that is wasted cost and not your job. Your sole remaining job is the one thing code cannot do: **semantic judgment** — hunting false-positive strengths and false-negative gaps.\n\n> ⛔ **YOU MAY NEVER WRITE `gap_analysis.json`.** It is owned by the Analyst. You only ever `ReadFile` it. Writing it — even to \"improve\" or \"rebuild\" it — is the single worst thing you can do; you would clobber the analysis you were asked to audit. The hostile-auditor mindset below is for finding problems to *report*, never to *rewrite*.\n>\n> ✍️ **Your only write target is `analyst_validator_verdict.json`** — a separate file you own, and the **source of truth** for your verdict. The Analyst reads this file (not your tool-return text) to decide APPROVE/FLAG/REJECT, and the server reads it to show the verdict in the UI. This file contains NO requirements/strengths/gaps — there is nothing in it to \"redo.\" Persisting a finding is not fixing.\n\n> 📂 **FILES ARE ON DISK — NOT IN YOUR CONTEXT.** The Analyst has already written `gap_analysis.json`, `candidate_profile.json`, and `enhanced_jd.json` to the workspace before calling you. They will **not** appear in your prompt or context — that is expected and correct. Your only way to see them is `ReadFile`. Never assume a file is missing because it is absent from context; `ReadFile` it.\n\n---\n\n## Core Principle\n\n**You are a hostile auditor and the candidate's ultimate defense attorney.** Your job is to critically evaluate the *quality* and *structure* of the Analyst's gap analysis. You must aggressively hunt for false positives (hallucinated strengths) and false negatives (lazy gaps).\n\nDo not attempt to fix errors yourself. Report specific structural and semantic problems with enough detail for the Analyst to fix them.\n\n---\n\n## Verdict Scale & Thresholds\n\n| Verdict | Condition |\n| --- | --- |\n| **REJECT** | 1 or more `blocking` **semantic** issues found (a hallucinated strength or a missed gap that must be overturned). |\n| **FLAG** | 0 `blocking` issues, but 1 or more `warning` issues found. |\n| **APPROVE** | 0 issues found. |\n\n(There is no structural REJECT anymore — structural defects are repaired deterministically by the server, not by your verdict.)\n\n---\n\n## CRITICAL: Execution Mode\n\n**⚠️ DO NOT NARRATE. DO NOT REASON ALOUD. EXECUTE IMMEDIATELY. ⚠️**\n\nYour **very first action** must be a `ReadFile` tool call. No reasoning preamble, no \"I will now...\", no \"Auditing inputs...\" — call the tool instantly.\n\n```\n✅ CORRECT:\n  [Silent] Call ReadFile(\"gap_analysis.json\")      ← FIRST ACTION, no text before this\n  [Silent] Call ReadFile(\"candidate_profile.json\")\n  [Silent] Call ReadFile(\"enhanced_jd.json\")\n  [Silent] Call ReadFile(\"cv_raw.txt\")             ← candidate's raw prose (for contradiction check)\n  [Silent] Call ReadFile(\"cover_letter_sample.txt\") ← optional; tolerate absence\n  [Silent] Perform the semantic audit (false positives / false negatives)\n  [Silent] WriteFile(\"analyst_validator_verdict.json\", ...) — your OWN file (Step 3), the source of truth; NEVER gap_analysis.json\n  [Output] One short completion line — the file holds the verdict (Step 4)\n\n❌ INCORRECT:\n  [Reasoning] \"I'm auditing the input files...\"\n  [Reasoning] \"Validating file contents...\"\n  [Reasoning] \"My current focus is on...\"\n  [Output] {\"verdict\": \"REJECT\", \"issues\": [{\"problem\": \"Files not provided in context\"}]}\n```\n\n**Never return a verdict citing missing files — the files already exist on disk, written by the Analyst before it called you. Their absence from your context is expected. Call ReadFile.**\n\n## ⛔ Banned Narration Phrases\n\nReason freely in your thinking — the semantic audit needs it. These phrases must not appear in your **output** (the completion line); they signal a no-op acknowledgment instead of a real audit:\n\n| Banned |\n|--------|\n| \"Auditing inputs\" / \"Auditing input files\" |\n| \"Validating file contents\" |\n| \"My current focus is on...\" |\n| \"I am continuing my deep dive...\" |\n| \"I'm meticulously examining...\" |\n| \"Before proceeding...\" |\n| \"I will now...\" / \"Next, I'll...\" |\n| Any progress update or status message |\n\n---\n\n## Execution Protocol\n\n### Step 1: Ingest Data\n\nCall `ReadFile` to load the following files before doing anything else:\n\n1. `ReadFile(\"gap_analysis.json\")`\n2. `ReadFile(\"candidate_profile.json\")`\n3. `ReadFile(\"enhanced_jd.json\")`\n4. `ReadFile(\"cv_raw.txt\")` — the candidate's raw, unedited prose. Needed for the Demonstrated Contradictions check (spelling/jargon/register): `candidate_profile.json` is cleaned/structured, so contradictions are only visible in the raw text.\n5. `ReadFile(\"cover_letter_sample.txt\")` — optional. If absent, that is fine; skip it and rely on `cv_raw.txt`. Do NOT flag its absence as an error.\n\n> ⛔ **SERVER-OWNED FIELDS:** Ignore `overall_fit_score`, `role_strictness`, and `fit_rationale` in `gap_analysis.json`. They will hold placeholders (e.g., `\"__FIT_SCORE__\"`). This is expected. Do not flag them as errors.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: The Semantic Audit (The Skeptic) — your only audit\n\nCritically evaluate the Analyst's mapping logic. If the logic is flawed, log a `semantic` issue.\n\n> Structural integrity (path resolution, duplicates, verbatim text, tier, mandatory_gate, counts) is **not your concern** — the server repairs all of it deterministically. Spend your whole budget on judgment: does the evidence actually prove the claim, and did the Analyst miss anything?\n\n1. **Attack the Strengths (Hunting False Positives):**\n* **The Rule:** The cited evidence must *objectively* prove the candidate meets the requirement.\n* **The Audit:** Read the `evidence_source` in the candidate's CV. Does it actually support the JD requirement?\n* *Example Flag (`blocking`):* The JD requires \"Enterprise Architecture\". The Analyst cited \"Junior Developer - assisted with design\". That is insufficient. Tell the Analyst to downgrade it to a Gap.\n* *Example Flag (`blocking`):* The Analyst accepted a self-proclaimed \"core competency\" tag as proof of a hard technical skill. Tell the Analyst to reject it unless there is demonstrated work history.\n* **Soft-Attribute Exception:** `soft_skills[]` and `core_competencies[]` ARE valid evidence for requirements that are themselves soft-attribute or interest-based — warmth, patience, communication, teamwork, cultural respect, collaboration, interpersonal skills, \"An interest in…\" requirements. Do NOT flag these as overreach. The hard-evidence rule above applies only to substantive knowledge claims and technical skills, not to soft attributes. If a JD requirement is for communication ability, teamwork, or interpersonal conduct, and the Analyst cited a `soft_skills[]` or `core_competencies[]` tag, that mapping is correct — do not create a blocking issue for it.\n* **Transferable tag is correct framing, not overreach:** A strength carrying `evidence_type: \"transferable\"` (conf ≤ 3, `impact: \"Low\"`) is the Analyst *honestly* marking a soft-attribute / out-of-domain match (e.g. retail cash handling for \"attention to detail\"). This is the desired behaviour — do NOT flag it as a false positive, and do NOT demand it be promoted to `direct`. Only flag a transferable strength if the path does not resolve, or if the requirement is a **substantive technical/knowledge** claim that should have been a Gap rather than a transferable match.\n* **Administrative items must not be strengths (`semantic`):** If `strengths[]` contains an employer-side check or post-hire condition (e.g. \"Verification of tertiary qualifications\", \"National Police Check\", \"probationary period\"), flag it — these are not candidate assets and belong in `requirements[]` only.\n* **Direct strengths must carry real domain evidence:** A strength tagged `evidence_type: \"direct\"` with `confidence_level >= 4` must rest on a credential, demonstrated domain experience, or a named tool. If a \"direct\" conf-4 strength actually rests on a soft-attribute/out-of-domain path, flag it (`semantic`) — it should be retagged `transferable` and de-weighted, not carried as a domain win.\n\n**Four hard overreach checks (all `blocking` when they fire). These target *overreach*, not honest `transferable` framing — never use them to reject a strength the Analyst already, correctly, tagged `transferable` / conf ≤ 3 / impact Low, nor a legitimate soft-attribute mapping (see the Soft-Attribute Exception above).**\n\n* **Demonstrated Contradictions:** reject a soft-skill strength when the candidate's *actual prose* (`cv_raw.txt` / `cover_letter_sample.txt`) demonstrates the opposite of the claim. e.g. a \"Written Communication\" / \"clear and persuasive communication\" strength when the prose has glaring spelling errors, impenetrable academic jargon for a non-specialist role, or dense/passive/bureaucratic language where clarity is required. Tell the Analyst to demote to a Gap. (This is why you read the raw prose — `candidate_profile.json` is cleaned and hides these.)\n* **Modifier Overreach:** strictly audit hierarchy and funding modifiers. If the JD requires \"Lead\" / \"External\" (e.g. lead investigator, external grants) and the candidate is only \"Assistant\" / \"Internal\", reject the full Strength and demand a downgrade or a partial-match notation — the modifier mismatch makes it not a clean win.\n* **Contextual Disparity:** do not allow mapping physical, retail, or gig-economy resilience/pressure onto highly specific corporate/executive soft skills. If the *context* of the evidence is entirely divorced from the *context* of the requirement, reject it and demand a Gap. (Distinguish from the legitimate transferable case: a properly tagged `transferable` conf-≤3 strength is fine; this check fires when such a leap is carried as a real match.)\n* **Academic Conflation:** if a JD requirement specifically demands professional, commercial, or industry experience, reject any Strength whose *sole* evidence is university coursework, academic labs, or capstone/student projects. Tell the Analyst to demote to a Gap and note \"Academic experience only\".\n\n\n2. **Defend the Gaps (Hunting False Negatives):**\n* **The Rule:** The Analyst must not claim a gap if the CV contains a clear semantic equivalent.\n* **The Audit:** Look at the `gaps[]` array. Scan the `candidate_profile.json` yourself. Did the Analyst miss something?\n* *Example Flag (`blocking`):* The Analyst flagged \"Agile Methodology\" as a gap. However, the candidate's work history explicitly lists \"Scrum Master\". Tell the Analyst to overturn this gap and promote it to a Strength.\n\n\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Write Your Verdict File (analyst_validator_verdict.json) — THE SOURCE OF TRUTH\n\nThis file **is** your verdict. The Analyst reads it (it no longer parses your text return) and the server reads it to show a verdict bubble in the UI. So write the full, final object here — verdict + every issue you found. This is a fresh full write of a small file you own — **not** a read-modify-write, and **not** `gap_analysis.json`.\n\nBuild this object and write it:\n```json\n{\n  \"verdict\": \"REJECT | FLAG | APPROVE\",\n  \"agent\": \"analyst\",\n  \"summary\": \"2 blocking + 0 warning issue(s).\",\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"field\": \"strengths[2]\",\n      \"problem\": \"JD requires 'Enterprise Architecture'; cited evidence is 'Junior Developer - assisted with design'. Insufficient — downgrade to a Gap.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"audience\": \"user\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"field\": \"gaps[1]\",\n      \"problem\": \"You flagged 'Agile' as a gap, but work_history[0] lists Scrum Master. Overturn this gap.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"audience\": \"user\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nField rules:\n- **`verdict`** — `REJECT` if ANY issue is `blocking`; `FLAG` if there are only `warning` issues; `APPROVE` if none.\n- **`issues[]`** — one entry per finding. `field` is the location (e.g. `strengths[2]`, `gaps[1]`, `req_5`). `problem` is the actionable, plainly-worded finding the Analyst acts on. `severity` is `blocking` (false-positive strength or false-negative gap the Analyst must fix) or `warning` (advisory only). On a clean APPROVE, `issues` is `[]`.\n- **`summary`** — short tally, e.g. `\"2 blocking + 0 warning issue(s).\"`.\n\n`WriteFile(\"analyst_validator_verdict.json\", JSON.stringify(verdictObj, null, 2))` — bare filename, stringified. **Never** name `gap_analysis.json` in a WriteFile call.\n\n**Audience tagging — decide per issue** (every issue is semantic now):\n\n| audience | When | `problem` phrasing |\n|---|---|---|\n| `\"user\"` | Something about the candidate's actual fit the applicant would want to know: thin/partial evidence on a claimed strength, a missed gap, evidence that only half-covers a requirement, a false-positive that should be a gap. | Plain, candidate-facing — describe the evidence finding. e.g. \"Communication: only verbal experience is evidenced; written communication isn't demonstrated in the CV.\" |\n| `\"internal\"` | Classification/tagging mechanics that don't change the candidate's story: \"retag direct→transferable\", \"move admin item out of strengths into requirements\". Dev-facing. | Keep the analyst-directed text. |\n\nRule of thumb: evidence-sufficiency findings → `user`; tagging/classification mechanics → `internal`.\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Tool Return — Just a Completion Signal\n\nYour verdict lives in the **file** you wrote in Step 3 — that is what the Analyst reads and what the server surfaces. The text you return from the tool call is **no longer parsed**; it only needs to unblock the Analyst's `await`. So after writing the file, return one short line, e.g.:\n\n```\ndone — verdict written to analyst_validator_verdict.json\n```\n\nNo JSON payload, no markdown fences, no requirement to make the text machine-parseable. The only hard rule: **write the file FIRST (Step 3), then return** — the Analyst reads the file the instant your tool call resolves, so the file must already be on disk.\n\n---\n\n## Strict Constraints\n\n1. **Never write `gap_analysis.json`:** It belongs to the Analyst — you only ReadFile it. Your sole WriteFile target is `analyst_validator_verdict.json`. If you ever find yourself building a `requirements`/`strengths`/`gaps` object, STOP — that is the Analyst's job; you are redoing the analysis, which is forbidden.\n2. **Never fix the output yourself:** Report issues and return them. The Analyst owns the retry loop and will apply your insights.\n3. **File before return:** The verdict file (Step 3) is the source of truth — write it before you return. The tool-return text is only a completion signal and is not parsed, so it cannot \"corrupt\" anything; just keep it to one short line.\n4. **No Routing:** Do not call `ChangeAgent` or `SwitchAgent`.\n5. **Semantic only:** Do not spend tokens re-checking paths, counts, tiers, or verbatim text — the server repairs those. Your value is judgment the code cannot do.","query":"","jsonResponse":false,"jsonFormat":"","jsonSchemaMode":"typescript","fileParser":"native","imageAspectRatio":"1:1","maxIterations":20,"reasoningEffort":"medium","allowFallbacks":true,"temperature":0},"service":{"name":"kemu.io.ai-agent","version":"1.9.1","title":"AI Agent","description":"Define AI agents and tools for automated workflows","processor":"js","widgetUI":true,"settingsUI":false,"eventEmitter":true,"ignoreParentEvents":false,"svgIcon":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<svg width=\"1200pt\" height=\"1200pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 1200 1200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n <path d=\"m875.64 681.36-189.72-82.801c-45.961-19.922-82.559-56.52-102.48-102.48l-82.801-189.72c-6.4805-14.762-27.359-14.762-33.719 0l-82.801 189.72c-20.039 45.961-56.641 82.559-102.48 102.48l-190.08 82.922c-14.641 6.4805-14.762 27.238 0 33.719l193.44 85.441c45.719 20.281 82.199 57 102 103.08l80.039 186.12c6.3594 14.762 27.359 14.879 33.84 0l82.68-189.6c19.922-45.84 56.52-82.441 102.48-102.48l189.72-82.801c14.762-6.3594 14.762-27.238 0-33.719zm-210.84-6.9609c-3 6.7188-9.6016 10.801-16.559 10.801-2.3984 0-4.8008-0.48047-7.1992-1.4414-64.078-28.078-114.72-78.719-142.68-142.8-4.0781-9.1211 0.12109-19.801 9.2383-23.762 9.1211-3.9609 19.68 0.23828 23.762 9.3594 24.238 55.68 68.398 99.84 124.08 124.2 9.1211 3.9609 13.32 14.52 9.3594 23.641z\"/>\n <path d=\"m1113.1 322.08-109.56-47.762c-26.52-11.641-47.641-32.762-59.281-59.281l-47.762-109.56c-3.7188-8.5195-15.84-8.5195-19.559 0l-47.762 109.56c-11.641 26.52-32.762 47.641-59.281 59.281l-109.68 47.879c-8.5195 3.7188-8.5195 15.719-0.12109 19.441l111.72 49.32c26.398 11.762 47.52 33 58.922 59.52l46.32 107.64c3.6016 8.5195 15.719 8.5195 19.441 0l47.762-109.44c11.641-26.52 32.762-47.641 59.281-59.281l109.56-47.762c8.5195-3.7188 8.5195-15.84 0-19.559zm-149.28 15.84c-3.4805 5.6406-9.3594 8.6406-15.48 8.6406-3.1211 0-6.3594-0.83984-9.2383-2.5195-24.84-15.121-45.359-34.922-61.199-59.16-5.3984-8.3984-3-19.441 5.2812-24.961 8.2812-5.3984 19.441-3.1211 24.84 5.2812 12.961 19.68 29.641 35.762 49.68 48 8.5195 5.1602 11.281 16.199 6.1211 24.719z\"/>\n</svg>\n","color":"#42a5f5","mdHelp":"/docs/help/service.md","customWidgets":[{"name":"Memory History","color":"#eac43e","description":"Provides a simple in-memory history manager for debugging purposes.","contents":"KMU-CB-v1{\"{#}mBE0gxc\":{\"id\":\"{#}mBE0gxc\",\"canvas\":{\"position\":{\"x\":2006,\"y\":726}},\"children\":[{\"childId\":\"{#}4M2WbT3\",\"sourcePort\":\"{#}mBE0gxc_innerOutput_inner-input-input1\",\"targetPort\":\"{#}4M2WbT3_input_agent\"}],\"state\":{\"description\":\"Provides a simple in-memory history manager for debugging purposes.\",\"inputs\":[{\"index\":0,\"label\":\"agent\",\"name\":\"input1\",\"type\":[5],\"position\":{\"x\":519,\"y\":291}}],\"outputs\":[],\"name\":\"Memory History\",\"type\":\"custom\",\"color\":\"#eac43e\",\"icon\":\"database\",\"canvasPosition\":{\"x\":0,\"y\":0},\"markdownHelp\":\"\",\"settings\":[],\"protocolVersion\":\"2\"},\"type\":\"widgetGroup\"},\"{#}4M2WbT3\":{\"id\":\"{#}4M2WbT3\",\"canvas\":{\"position\":{\"x\":659,\"y\":341}},\"children\":[{\"childId\":\"{#}jCnteeA\",\"sourcePort\":\"{#}4M2WbT3_output_getHistory\",\"targetPort\":\"{#}jCnteeA_input_read\"},{\"childId\":\"{#}jCnteeA\",\"sourcePort\":\"{#}4M2WbT3_output_updateHistory\",\"targetPort\":\"{#}jCnteeA_input_update\"}],\"state\":{\"dynamicInputs\":{},\"dynamicOutputs\":{},\"customState\":{\"includeAttachments\":false,\"timeout\":60},\"variantId\":\"history\",\"service\":{\"name\":\"kemu.io.ai-agent\",\"version\":\"0.1.0\",\"title\":\"AI Agent\",\"description\":\"Define AI agents and tools for automated workflows\",\"processor\":\"js\",\"widgetUI\":true,\"settingsUI\":false,\"eventEmitter\":false,\"ignoreParentEvents\":false,\"svgIcon\":\"<svg fill=\\\"none\\\" xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\">\\n  <!-- AI Agent icon - brain/robot head -->\\n  <path d=\\\"M12 2C8.13 2 5 5.13 5 9c0 2.38 1.19 4.47 3 5.74V17c0 .55.45 1 1 1h6c.55 0 1-.45 1-1v-2.26c1.81-1.27 3-3.36 3-5.74 0-3.87-3.13-7-7-7z\\\" fill=\\\"currentColor\\\"/>\\n  <circle cx=\\\"9.5\\\" cy=\\\"9\\\" r=\\\"1.5\\\" fill=\\\"white\\\"/>\\n  <circle cx=\\\"14.5\\\" cy=\\\"9\\\" r=\\\"1.5\\\" fill=\\\"white\\\"/>\\n  <path d=\\\"M12 12c-.83 0-1.5-.67-1.5-1.5s.67-1.5 1.5-1.5 1.5.67 1.5 1.5-.67 1.5-1.5 1.5z\\\" fill=\\\"white\\\"/>\\n  <rect x=\\\"10\\\" y=\\\"19\\\" width=\\\"4\\\" height=\\\"3\\\" rx=\\\"1\\\" fill=\\\"currentColor\\\"/>\\n</svg>\",\"color\":\"#42a5f5\",\"inputs\":[{\"name\":\"query\",\"description\":\"Query string for the agent\",\"type\":1},{\"name\":\"attachments\",\"description\":\"Attachments for the agent (String, BinaryFile, ImageData, or Array of these types)\",\"type\":[1,12,7,3]},{\"name\":\"clear\",\"description\":\"Clear input signal\",\"type\":6},{\"name\":\"abort\",\"description\":\"Abort current query signal\",\"type\":6},{\"name\":\"send\",\"description\":\"Send input signal\",\"type\":6}],\"outputs\":[{\"name\":\"tools\",\"type\":5},{\"name\":\"history\",\"type\":5},{\"name\":\"json\",\"type\":5},{\"name\":\"text\",\"type\":1},{\"name\":\"stream\",\"type\":1},{\"name\":\"images\",\"description\":\"Generated images as ImageData array\",\"type\":3}],\"supportedPlatforms\":[\"win-x86\",\"win-x64\",\"osx-x64\",\"osx-arm64\",\"linux-debian-arm64\",\"linux-debian-x64\",\"linux-rhel-arm64\",\"linux-rhel-x64\"],\"author\":\"db618814-4e68-40aa-8158-64a595fea23b\",\"defaultVariantInfo\":{\"title\":\"Agent\",\"shortTitle\":\"Agent\",\"description\":\"AI agent that processes queries with system instructions and attachments\"},\"variants\":[{\"id\":\"tool\",\"name\":\"Tool\",\"description\":\"Define tools with arguments and results for AI agents\",\"svgIcon\":\"<svg fill=\\\"none\\\" xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\">\\n  <!-- Tool icon - wrench/settings -->\\n  <path d=\\\"M22.7 19l-9.1-9.1c.9-2.3.4-5-1.5-6.9-2-2-5-2.4-7.4-1.3L9 6 6 9 1.6 4.7C.4 7.1.9 10.1 2.9 12.1c1.9 1.9 4.6 2.4 6.9 1.5l9.1 9.1c.4.4 1 .4 1.4 0l2.3-2.3c.5-.4.5-1.1.1-1.4z\\\" fill=\\\"currentColor\\\"/>\\n</svg>\\n\",\"inputs\":[{\"name\":\"input\",\"description\":\"Tool input data\",\"type\":5}],\"outputs\":[{\"name\":\"arguments\",\"description\":\"Tool arguments\",\"type\":5}],\"color\":\"#42a5f5\"},{\"id\":\"submit\",\"name\":\"Submit\",\"description\":\"Submit data without any processing\",\"svgIcon\":\"<svg fill=\\\"none\\\" xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\">\\n  <!-- Submit icon - send/arrow -->\\n  <path d=\\\"M2.01 21L23 12 2.01 3 2 10l15 2-15 2z\\\" fill=\\\"currentColor\\\"/>\\n</svg>\\n\",\"inputs\":[{\"name\":\"input\",\"description\":\"Data to submit\",\"type\":6}],\"color\":\"#68bb6c\"},{\"id\":\"history\",\"name\":\"History\",\"description\":\"Manage conversation history and session storage for AI agents\",\"svgIcon\":\"<svg fill=\\\"none\\\" xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 16 16\\\">\\n  <path\\n    d=\\\"M8 1.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13zM0 8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8z\\\"\\n    fill=\\\"white\\\"\\n  />\\n  <path\\n    d=\\\"M8 3.5a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v4l2.5 1.5a.5.5 0 0 1-.5.866L7.5 8.866A.5.5 0 0 1 7.5 8V4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5z\\\"\\n    fill=\\\"white\\\"\\n  />\\n  <path\\n    d=\\\"M2.5 8a5.5 5.5 0 0 1 5.5-5.5V1A7 7 0 0 0 1 8h1.5z\\\"\\n    fill=\\\"white\\\"\\n  />\\n</svg>\\n\",\"inputs\":[{\"name\":\"agent\",\"description\":\"Connect to the agent\",\"type\":5}],\"outputs\":[{\"name\":\"getHistory\",\"description\":\"Invoked when the agent needs to retrieve the conversation history\",\"type\":5},{\"name\":\"updateHistory\",\"description\":\"Invoked when the agent needs to update the conversation history\",\"type\":5}],\"color\":\"#9c27b0\"}],\"internal\":false,\"devMode\":true,\"sessionId\":1760512532}},\"type\":\"hubService\",\"groupId\":\"{#}mBE0gxc\"},\"{#}a5vxU9Y\":{\"id\":\"{#}a5vxU9Y\",\"canvas\":{\"position\":{\"x\":1235,\"y\":488}},\"children\":[],\"state\":{\"dynamicInputs\":{},\"dynamicOutputs\":{},\"customState\":{},\"variantId\":\"submit\",\"service\":{\"name\":\"kemu.io.ai-agent\",\"version\":\"0.1.0\",\"title\":\"AI Agent\",\"description\":\"Define AI agents and tools for automated workflows\",\"processor\":\"js\",\"widgetUI\":true,\"settingsUI\":false,\"eventEmitter\":false,\"ignoreParentEvents\":false,\"svgIcon\":\"<svg fill=\\\"none\\\" xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\">\\n  <!-- AI Agent icon - brain/robot head -->\\n  <path d=\\\"M12 2C8.13 2 5 5.13 5 9c0 2.38 1.19 4.47 3 5.74V17c0 .55.45 1 1 1h6c.55 0 1-.45 1-1v-2.26c1.81-1.27 3-3.36 3-5.74 0-3.87-3.13-7-7-7z\\\" fill=\\\"currentColor\\\"/>\\n  <circle cx=\\\"9.5\\\" cy=\\\"9\\\" r=\\\"1.5\\\" fill=\\\"white\\\"/>\\n  <circle cx=\\\"14.5\\\" cy=\\\"9\\\" r=\\\"1.5\\\" fill=\\\"white\\\"/>\\n  <path d=\\\"M12 12c-.83 0-1.5-.67-1.5-1.5s.67-1.5 1.5-1.5 1.5.67 1.5 1.5-.67 1.5-1.5 1.5z\\\" fill=\\\"white\\\"/>\\n  <rect x=\\\"10\\\" y=\\\"19\\\" width=\\\"4\\\" height=\\\"3\\\" rx=\\\"1\\\" fill=\\\"currentColor\\\"/>\\n</svg>\",\"color\":\"#42a5f5\",\"inputs\":[{\"name\":\"query\",\"description\":\"Query string for the agent\",\"type\":1},{\"name\":\"attachments\",\"description\":\"Attachments for the agent (String, BinaryFile, ImageData, or Array of these types)\",\"type\":[1,12,7,3]},{\"name\":\"clear\",\"description\":\"Clear input signal\",\"type\":6},{\"name\":\"abort\",\"description\":\"Abort current query signal\",\"type\":6},{\"name\":\"send\",\"description\":\"Send input signal\",\"type\":6}],\"outputs\":[{\"name\":\"tools\",\"type\":5},{\"name\":\"history\",\"type\":5},{\"name\":\"json\",\"type\":5},{\"name\":\"text\",\"type\":1},{\"name\":\"stream\",\"type\":1},{\"name\":\"images\",\"description\":\"Generated images as ImageData array\",\"type\":3}],\"supportedPlatforms\":[\"win-x86\",\"win-x64\",\"osx-x64\",\"osx-arm64\",\"linux-debian-arm64\",\"linux-debian-x64\",\"linux-rhel-arm64\",\"linux-rhel-x64\"],\"author\":\"db618814-4e68-40aa-8158-64a595fea23b\",\"defaultVariantInfo\":{\"title\":\"Agent\",\"shortTitle\":\"Agent\",\"description\":\"AI agent that processes queries with system instructions and attachments\"},\"variants\":[{\"id\":\"tool\",\"name\":\"Tool\",\"description\":\"Define tools with arguments and results for AI agents\",\"svgIcon\":\"<svg fill=\\\"none\\\" xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\">\\n  <!-- Tool icon - wrench/settings -->\\n  <path d=\\\"M22.7 19l-9.1-9.1c.9-2.3.4-5-1.5-6.9-2-2-5-2.4-7.4-1.3L9 6 6 9 1.6 4.7C.4 7.1.9 10.1 2.9 12.1c1.9 1.9 4.6 2.4 6.9 1.5l9.1 9.1c.4.4 1 .4 1.4 0l2.3-2.3c.5-.4.5-1.1.1-1.4z\\\" fill=\\\"currentColor\\\"/>\\n</svg>\\n\",\"inputs\":[{\"name\":\"input\",\"description\":\"Tool input data\",\"type\":5}],\"outputs\":[{\"name\":\"arguments\",\"description\":\"Tool arguments\",\"type\":5}],\"color\":\"#42a5f5\"},{\"id\":\"submit\",\"name\":\"Submit\",\"description\":\"Submit data without any processing\",\"svgIcon\":\"<svg fill=\\\"none\\\" xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\">\\n  <!-- Submit icon - send/arrow -->\\n  <path d=\\\"M2.01 21L23 12 2.01 3 2 10l15 2-15 2z\\\" fill=\\\"currentColor\\\"/>\\n</svg>\\n\",\"inputs\":[{\"name\":\"input\",\"description\":\"Data to submit\",\"type\":6}],\"color\":\"#68bb6c\"},{\"id\":\"history\",\"name\":\"History\",\"description\":\"Manage conversation history and session storage for AI agents\",\"svgIcon\":\"<svg fill=\\\"none\\\" xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 16 16\\\">\\n  <path\\n    d=\\\"M8 1.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13zM0 8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8z\\\"\\n    fill=\\\"white\\\"\\n  />\\n  <path\\n    d=\\\"M8 3.5a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v4l2.5 1.5a.5.5 0 0 1-.5.866L7.5 8.866A.5.5 0 0 1 7.5 8V4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5z\\\"\\n    fill=\\\"white\\\"\\n  />\\n  <path\\n    d=\\\"M2.5 8a5.5 5.5 0 0 1 5.5-5.5V1A7 7 0 0 0 1 8h1.5z\\\"\\n    fill=\\\"white\\\"\\n  />\\n</svg>\\n\",\"inputs\":[{\"name\":\"agent\",\"description\":\"Connect to the agent\",\"type\":5}],\"outputs\":[{\"name\":\"getHistory\",\"description\":\"Invoked when the agent needs to retrieve the conversation history\",\"type\":5},{\"name\":\"updateHistory\",\"description\":\"Invoked when the agent needs to update the conversation history\",\"type\":5}],\"color\":\"#9c27b0\"}],\"internal\":false,\"devMode\":true,\"sessionId\":1760512532}},\"type\":\"hubService\",\"secrets\":{\"OPENROUTER_API_KEY\":{\"name\":\"OPENROUTER_API_KEY\",\"hubServiceName\":\"kemu.io.ai-agent\"}},\"groupId\":\"{#}mBE0gxc\"},\"{#}jCnteeA\":{\"id\":\"{#}jCnteeA\",\"canvas\":{\"position\":{\"x\":948,\"y\":397}},\"children\":[{\"childId\":\"{#}a5vxU9Y\",\"sourcePort\":\"{#}jCnteeA_output_sessionHistoryOutput\",\"targetPort\":\"{#}a5vxU9Y_input_input\"}],\"state\":{\"pauseExecution\":false,\"autoPauseOnError\":true,\"version\":2,\"metadata\":{\"name\":\"Memory History\",\"description\":\"Keeps the history messages in memory (this is intended for dev purposes only)\"},\"pages\":{\"main\":{\"code\":\"/**\\n * Name: Memory History\\n * Description: Keeps the history messages in memory (this is intended for dev purposes only)\\n */\\n\\nconst sessions = {};\\n\\nconst getWidgetInputs = () => [\\n  { name: 'read', type: DataType.JsonObj },\\n  { name: 'update', type: [DataType.JsonObj, DataType.Array] }\\n];\\n\\nconst getWidgetOutputs = () => [\\n  { name: 'sessionHistoryOutput', type: DataType.JsonObj }\\n];\\n\\nconst onParentEvent = async ({ targetPort, event }) => {\\n  const inputData = event.data.value;\\n\\n  if (targetPort.name === 'read') {\\n    const sessionId = inputData.sessionId;\\n\\n    if (sessionId === undefined || sessionId === null) {\\n      console.error(\\\"Error: 'read' event missing 'sessionId' property.\\\");\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    if (!sessions[sessionId]) {\\n      sessions[sessionId] = { messages: [] };\\n    }\\n\\n    await setOutput({ port: 'sessionHistoryOutput', data: { type: DataType.JsonObj, value: sessions[sessionId] } });\\n\\n  } else if (targetPort.name === 'update') {\\n    const sessionId = inputData.sessionId;\\n    const messagesToProcess = inputData.messages;\\n\\n    if (sessionId === undefined || sessionId === null) {\\n      console.error(\\\"Error: 'update' event missing 'sessionId' property.\\\");\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (messagesToProcess === undefined || messagesToProcess === null) {\\n      console.error(\\\"Error: 'update' event missing 'messagesToAdd' property. No messages to add.\\\");\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    if (!sessions[sessionId]) {\\n      sessions[sessionId] = { messages: [] };\\n    }\\n\\n    if (Array.isArray(messagesToProcess)) {\\n      sessions[sessionId].messages.push(...messagesToProcess);\\n    } else {\\n      sessions[sessionId].messages.push(messagesToProcess);\\n    }\\n  }\\n};\",\"language\":\"javascript\",\"name\":\"My First Script\"}}},\"type\":\"script\",\"secrets\":{},\"groupId\":\"{#}mBE0gxc\"}}","rootGroupId":"{#}mBE0gxc","icon":"database","protocolVersion":"2"}],"inputs":[{"name":"config","description":"Configuration object containing query, attachments, sessionId, and systemInstructions. Can also be a string to be used as query or a boolean to trigger processing.","type":[5,4,1,6]},{"name":"abort","description":"Abort current query signal","type":6}],"outputs":[{"name":"tools","type":5},{"name":"history","type":5},{"name":"json","type":5},{"name":"text","type":1},{"name":"stream","type":1},{"name":"reasoning","description":"Reasoning output from models that support extended thinking","type":1},{"name":"images","description":"Generated images as ImageData array","type":3},{"name":"debug","description":"Includes debugging information for when things go wrong, including stopping reason","type":5}],"supportedPlatforms":["win-x86","win-x64","osx-x64","osx-arm64","linux-debian-arm64","linux-debian-x64","linux-rhel-arm64","linux-rhel-x64"],"author":"0f998d5a-a8ce-4bf8-9f84-fa8c481cb40b","defaultVariantInfo":{"title":"Agent","shortTitle":"Agent","description":"AI agent that processes queries with system instructions and attachments"},"variants":[{"id":"chatInterface","name":"Chat Interface","description":"Chat window UI that can invoke an Agent and display live outputs","svgIcon":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<svg width=\"1200pt\" height=\"1200pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 1200 1200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n <path d=\"m1034.4 486-298.78-46.781v244.78c0 26.391-10.781 50.391-31.219 67.219-15.609 14.391-36 21.609-57.609 21.609-4.7812 0-9.6094 0-14.391-1.2188l-134.39-20.391v80.391c0 15.609 7.2188 30 18 39.609 12 10.781 27.609 14.391 43.219 12l309.61-48h8.4375c1.2188 0 1.2188 1.2188 2.3906 1.2188 1.2188 1.2188 2.3906 1.2188 3.6094 2.3906l111.61 96-4.7812-103.22v-4.8281c0-1.2188 1.2188-3.6094 2.3906-4.7812 0-1.2188 0-1.2188 1.2188-1.2188 1.2188-1.2188 1.2188-1.2188 2.3906-2.3906 1.2188 0 1.2188-1.2188 2.3906-1.2188 1.2188 0 1.2188-1.2188 3.6094-1.2188 1.2188 0 1.2188-1.2188 2.3906-1.2188l28.781-4.7812c26.391-3.6094 45.609-26.391 45.609-52.781l-0.09375-217.18c1.2188-26.391-18-49.219-44.391-54z\"/>\n <